+- Removing a user from an organization (`DELETE /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}`, for offboarding):
+  - Only org admins of that organization may do it; other callers get 403.
+  - An organization other than the caller's → 404. A user who does not exist or is not in
+    that organization → 404.
+  - The user's memberships in all of the organization's projects are deleted, and the tasks
+    they were assigned in those projects are unassigned. The whole change is all-or-nothing.
+  - This is allowed in archived projects too, so that a departing user loses access to them.
+  - The user's organization and org admin flag are not changed, so an org admin who leaves
+    keeps org admin rights until those are cleared separately.
+  - Removing a user who has no memberships is still 204.
 
